{"type":"message","id":"a623b7d9","parentId":"f1f9544b","timestamp":"2026-07-03T16:11:22.209Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so:\n1. TH keyword \"กิ๊บตึ๊ง ผ้าไหม\" returned non-hair-clip results (iPhone, iPad, etc.) - the keyword search on TH is returning results from other categories because the API nodeId filter is broken for TH\n2. VN keyword \"kẹp tóc 2025\" returned cosmetics and other unrelated items - also not filtering properly\n\nThe TH API seems to not support the hair accessories category at all through the keyword filter. Let me try with a more specific Thai hair clip keyword.\n\nActually wait - looking at the TH data more carefully, it returned 42 pages and the top results are all electronics/phones. \n\nThe search is clearly broken for Thai hair accessories. I'll try a different approach with a more targeted keyword like \"คลิปหนีบผม\" for hair clips, and if that doesn't work, I'll use the Vietnamese results I've already gathered. Looking at the Vietnamese data, I've identified some strong performers like a claw clip with significant sales growth, a large bow clip with recent listing, and an office bun clip option.\n\nNow I'm cross-referencing these against the v8.0 criteria which requires items listed within the last six months, and I'm noticing some candidates exceed that threshold—several from 2025 fall outside the window, while more recent ones from April and May 2026 qualify.\n\nLooking at the candidates that meet the timeline, I'm scoring them based on sales volume and growth metrics, starting with the Valley Limit bear clip which shows 72 monthly sales with a perfect 5.0 rating despite limited review count, and the satin flower bud bun clip which has 60 monthly sales.\n\nContinuing through the remaining clips, I'm seeing stronger performers like the AISHG triangle denim heart clip with solid 74% growth and a 4.92 rating, though it only has 6 seven-day sales. The TMR bun clip stands out with exceptional 405% growth and strong monthly volume, while the custom name font clip shows impressive 213% growth despite lower overall sales numbers.\n\nBut I'm realizing the upload date check isn't working properly in the API—the category search returns results ranked by sales volume, which filters out newer uploads that haven't accumulated enough sales yet. The Vietnamese haircap market sits around $1-2 USD, so I need to adjust my price expectations accordingly. Let me try a different search approach to capture fresh uploads, or I could pivot to using TikTok data through FastMoss instead since the standard API isn't giving me what I need. 3. Use Google search to find trending hair clips in Vietnam/Thailand\n\nActually, let me try searching TikTok data since that was part of the task request. Let me try to use the tiktok search or similar.\n\nBut first, let me also try a more targeted approach for TH. Let me try the TH API with a different keyword.\n\nActually, I think the most honest approach given the time constraint is:\n\n1. Use the VN data I have (Sorftime API is working)\n2. Try TH with another keyword search\n3. If TH data is unavailable via API, I'll note the gap and try to find TH hair clip data through another method\n\nLet me try the TH keyword \"คลิปหนีบ\" which is \"hair clip\" in Thai.\n\nI should also pull FastMoss data for TikTok insights, and check the TK verification on some of these top-performing items.","thinkingSignature":"4e8186993e53e40c4f3886beb897b4a7953453877e93ff35180eae3a191f751e"},{"type":"text","text":"关键词搜索 TH 失败（API 返回全类目）。用泰语精准词再试，并同步验证 TikTok。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_nymwv1eedxlu_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST 'https://mcp.sorftime.com/' \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer rhblyi…qt09\" \\\n  -H 'accept: application/json, text/event-stream' \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"tools/call\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"shopee_product_search\",\"arguments\":{